From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nowon <nowon@noreply.pepecoin.surf>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 18:12:58 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 130/144] GreatDANE: fail the trademark check on Pepecoin
 publisher strings and require the Support label (round 4g)

trademark_userfacing_check.py now asserts:

- unofficial About uses dane-bottom-links-support = "Support" at
  https://dane.surf/support/
- official branding keeps bottom-links-terms = "Terms of Use" and the
  Firefox terms URL
- unofficial donate stays absent; official helpus donate stays
- module.ver company is Dane and copyright is Dane contributors, with the
  Mozilla.org trademark credit
- branding.nsi CompanyName is Dane, and CertNameDownload / CertIssuerDownload
  are the TODO-NO-WINDOWS-SIGNING-IDENTITY-YET placeholders with the comment
  that no Windows signing identity exists yet and the publisher name is the
  owner's decision
- any Pepecoin publisher/company string in Windows metadata (module.ver,
  manifests, branding.nsi) is a failure

pepecoin.surf update URLs are not treated as publisher strings. No build, no
signing, no network.

Prepared only. Not built, signed, notarized or published.
